
# Objects in JavaScript

Objects are used to store multiple values in a single variable using key-value pairs.

An object can contain:
- Properties
- Methods

# Why Use Objects?
Objects help organize related data together.

Example:
A student object can store:
- Name
- Age
- Course

instead of creating separate variables.
# Creating an Object

## Syntax
let objectName = {
    key: value
};


## Accessing Object Properties

There are two ways:
Dot Notation
Bracket Notation

Dot Notation
console.log(student.name);
Output:
Sudarshan

Bracket Notation
console.log(student["age"]);
Output:
21

## Modifying Object Properties
student.age = 22;

console.log(student.age);

Output:
22

# Adding New Properties
student.city = "Bangalore";

console.log(student);
Deleting Properties
delete student.course;

console.log(student);

## Properties in JavaScript

Properties are values associated with objects.

Example:

let car = {
    brand: "BMW",
    color: "Black"
};

Here:

brand is a property
color is a property


## Data Properties

->Data properties store values inside objects.

Example:

let employee = {
    name: "Rahul",
    salary: 50000
};


Data Property Attributes

Each property has attributes like:
value
writable
enumerable
configurable